# 🔄 Project Workflow — Ice Cream Parlour Management System

## 1. 🎯 Main Objective

The Ice Cream Parlour Management System is a Java-based application designed to digitize and simplify the daily operations of an ice cream parlour using Core Java, JDBC, MySQL, and the DAO (Data Access Object) design pattern.

The system provides two main modules: **Customer** and **Admin**. Customers can browse menu categories, select products, manage their cart, place orders, and receive bills. Administrators can authenticate themselves to manage menu items, maintain inventory, view orders, and access sales information.

The DAO architecture separates database access operations from application logic, improving code organization, reusability, and maintainability without requiring changes to the existing MySQL database schema.

